      "source": [
        "# SpaceX Falcon 9 — First-Stage Landing Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "## Consolidated Capstone Project Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "### Project Objective\n",
        "The objective is to analyze Falcon 9 launches and develop classification models that estimate whether the first stage will land successfully. Reusing the first stage is an important factor in launch economics: reliable predictions can help assess mission risk and understand factors associated with rocket recovery.\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook brings together the data-wrangling, exploratory analysis, SQL, geographic visualization, interactive dashboard, and machine-learning labs. Conclusions should be based on results obtained by running the cells, not on assumptions.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Table of Contents\n",
        "1. [Data Wrangling](#section-data-wrangling)\n",
        "2. [EDA and Feature Engineering](#section-eda-feature-engineering)\n",
        "3. [SQL: Exploratory Analysis](#section-sql)\n",
        "4. [Geographic Visualization with Folium](#section-folium)\n",
        "5. [Interactive Dashboard with Plotly Dash](#section-plotly-dash)\n",
        "6. [Machine Learning Prediction](#section-machine-learning)\n",
        "7. [Overall Conclusion and Final Checklist](#conclusion-general)\n"
      ]
    },
